    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-issues-act-2005-sch-1-sec-2",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "2 Transitional—clauses 14 and 15 of Schedule 1 to the",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-issues-act-2005#sch-1-sec-2"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-issues-act-2005.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-issues-act-2005.pdf, p.8",
      "values:originalText": "Telecommunications Act 1997\n(1)\nFor the purposes of this item, a pre-commencement reporting period is:\n\n(a) a financial year that:\n\n(i) began on or after 1 July 1997; and\n\n(ii) ended before the commencement of this item; or\n\n(b) if this item does not commence on a 1 July in any financial\nyear—the period:\n\n(i) beginning at the start of the financial year in which this\nitem commenced; and\n\n(ii) ending immediately before the commencement of this\nitem.\n(2)\nDespite the amendment made by item 1, clauses 14 and 15 of\nSchedule 1 to the Telecommunications Act 1997 continue to apply as if:\n\n(a) each reference in those clauses to a financial year were a\nreference to a pre-commencement reporting period; and\n\n(b) the amendment had not been made.\n\nIndustry codes  Schedule 2\n\nTelecommunications Legislation Amendment (Competition and Consumer Issues) Act 2005\nNo. 119, 2005            5",
      "skos:definition": "Telecommunications Act 1997\n(1)\nFor the purposes of this item, a pre-commencement reporting period is:\n\n(a) a financial year that:\n\n(i) began on or after 1 July 1997; and\n\n(ii) ended before the commencement of this item; or\n\n(b) if this item does not commence on a 1 July in any financial\nyear—the period:\n\n(i) beginning at the start of the financial year in which this\nitem commenced; and\n\n(ii) ending immediately before the commencement of this\nitem.\n(2)\nDespite the amendment made by item 1, clauses 14 and 15 of\nSchedule 1 to the Telecommunications Act 1997 continue to apply as if:\n\n(a) each reference in those clauses to a financial year were a\nreference to a pre-commencement reporting period; and\n\n(b) the amendment had not been made.\n\nIndustry codes  Schedule 2\n\nTelecommunications Legislation Amendment (Competition and Consumer Issues) Act 2005\nNo. 119, 2005            5",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-issues-act-2005-sch-1-sec-2-norm"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "ef326c14dabefa0eb0dc6fae5486a1784f2df07736134a3ba75693d36ce0920b",
      "skos:note": "Defines pre-commencement reporting period for transitional provisions."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-issues-act-2005#sch-1-sec-2",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "2 Transitional—clauses 14 and 15 of Schedule 1 to the",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 8,
      "values:originalText": "Telecommunications Act 1997\n(1)\nFor the purposes of this item, a pre-commencement reporting period is:\n\n(a) a financial year that:\n\n(i) began on or after 1 July 1997; and\n\n(ii) ended before the commencement of this item; or\n\n(b) if this item does not commence on a 1 July in any financial\nyear—the period:\n\n(i) beginning at the start of the financial year in which this\nitem commenced; and\n\n(ii) ending immediately before the commencement of this\nitem.\n(2)\nDespite the amendment made by item 1, clauses 14 and 15 of\nSchedule 1 to the Telecommunications Act 1997 continue to apply as if:\n\n(a) each reference in those clauses to a financial year were a\nreference to a pre-commencement reporting period; and\n\n(b) the amendment had not been made.\n\nIndustry codes  Schedule 2\n\nTelecommunications Legislation Amendment (Competition and Consumer Issues) Act 2005\nNo. 119, 2005            5"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-issues-act-2005-sch-1-sec-2-norm",
      "@type": "values:Undertaking",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-issues-act-2005-sch-1-sec-2"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-issues-act-2005-sch-2-sec-1",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "1 After subsection 121(1A)",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-issues-act-2005#sch-2-sec-1"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-issues-act-2005.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-issues-act-2005.pdf, p.9",
      "values:originalText": "Insert:\n\n(1B) If:\n\n(a) at a time when an industry code (the original code) was\nregistered under this Part, a direction could have been given\nto a person under subsection (1) in respect of the original\ncode; and\n\n(b) the original code has been replaced by another code that is\nregistered under this Part; and\n\n(c) the person could have been given a direction under\nsubsection (1) in respect of the replacement code, if the\nconduct concerned had occurred after the replacement code\nwas registered;\nthen, during the period when the replacement code is registered\nunder this Part, the person may be given a direction under\nsubsection (1) in respect of the replacement code.",
      "skos:definition": "Insert:\n\n(1B) If:\n\n(a) at a time when an industry code (the original code) was\nregistered under this Part, a direction could have been given\nto a person under subsection (1) in respect of the original\ncode; and\n\n(b) the original code has been replaced by another code that is\nregistered under this Part; and\n\n(c) the person could have been given a direction under\nsubsection (1) in respect of the replacement code, if the\nconduct concerned had occurred after the replacement code\nwas registered;\nthen, during the period when the replacement code is registered\nunder this Part, the person may be given a direction under\nsubsection (1) in respect of the replacement code.",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-issues-act-2005-sch-2-sec-1-norm"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "8e1f59dcbeb8ac13e59cd39563f1fc29b95e4eac571c2a029ce0a87857dd2e12",
      "skos:note": "Person may be given direction under subsection (1) in respect of replacement code during period when replacement code is registered."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-issues-act-2005#sch-2-sec-1",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "1 After subsection 121(1A)",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 9,
      "values:originalText": "Insert:\n\n(1B) If:\n\n(a) at a time when an industry code (the original code) was\nregistered under this Part, a direction could have been given\nto a person under subsection (1) in respect of the original\ncode; and\n\n(b) the original code has been replaced by another code that is\nregistered under this Part; and\n\n(c) the person could have been given a direction under\nsubsection (1) in respect of the replacement code, if the\nconduct concerned had occurred after the replacement code\nwas registered;\nthen, during the period when the replacement code is registered\nunder this Part, the person may be given a direction under\nsubsection (1) in respect of the replacement code."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-issues-act-2005-sch-2-sec-1-norm",
      "@type": "values:Permission",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
