    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-issues-act-2005-sch-7-sec-14-2",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "14 After subsection 152BZ(2)",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-issues-act-2005#sch-7-sec-14-2"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-issues-act-2005.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-issues-act-2005.pdf, p.18",
      "values:originalText": "Insert:\n\n(2A) If:\n\n(a) the Procedural Rules make provision for or in relation to a\ntime limit for giving the information; and\n\n(b) the carrier or provider does not give the Commission the\ninformation within the time limit allowed by the Procedural\nRules;\nthe Commission may, by written notice given to the carrier or\nprovider, reject the variation.\n\n(2B) Subsection (2A) has effect despite anything in this Division.\n\nProcedural Rules  Schedule 7\n\nTelecommunications Legislation Amendment (Competition and Consumer Issues) Act 2005\nNo. 119, 2005            15\n\n(2C) If the Commission makes a decision under subsection (2A) to\nreject the variation, subsection 152BY(7) has effect as if the\ndecision had been made under subsection 152BY(3).",
      "skos:definition": "Insert:\n\n(2A) If:\n\n(a) the Procedural Rules make provision for or in relation to a\ntime limit for giving the information; and\n\n(b) the carrier or provider does not give the Commission the\ninformation within the time limit allowed by the Procedural\nRules;\nthe Commission may, by written notice given to the carrier or\nprovider, reject the variation.\n\n(2B) Subsection (2A) has effect despite anything in this Division.\n\nProcedural Rules  Schedule 7\n\nTelecommunications Legislation Amendment (Competition and Consumer Issues) Act 2005\nNo. 119, 2005            15\n\n(2C) If the Commission makes a decision under subsection (2A) to\nreject the variation, subsection 152BY(7) has effect as if the\ndecision had been made under subsection 152BY(3).",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-issues-act-2005-sch-7-sec-14-2-ss-2a"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-issues-act-2005-sch-7-sec-14-2-ss-2b"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-issues-act-2005-sch-7-sec-14-2-ss-2c"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "8445d5cfe714f4491bdd7be3a32948e53e2a96ef2d6d75ca8d501fbc73a359c4"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-issues-act-2005#sch-7-sec-14-2",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "14 After subsection 152BZ(2)",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 18,
      "values:originalText": "Insert:\n\n(2A) If:\n\n(a) the Procedural Rules make provision for or in relation to a\ntime limit for giving the information; and\n\n(b) the carrier or provider does not give the Commission the\ninformation within the time limit allowed by the Procedural\nRules;\nthe Commission may, by written notice given to the carrier or\nprovider, reject the variation.\n\n(2B) Subsection (2A) has effect despite anything in this Division.\n\nProcedural Rules  Schedule 7\n\nTelecommunications Legislation Amendment (Competition and Consumer Issues) Act 2005\nNo. 119, 2005            15\n\n(2C) If the Commission makes a decision under subsection (2A) to\nreject the variation, subsection 152BY(7) has effect as if the\ndecision had been made under subsection 152BY(3)."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-issues-act-2005-sch-7-sec-14-2-ss-2a",
