    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-issues-act-2005-sch-10-sec-572b",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "572B Acceptance of undertakings",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-issues-act-2005#sch-10-sec-572b"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-issues-act-2005.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-issues-act-2005.pdf, p.30",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The ACMA may accept any of the following undertakings:\n\n(a) a written undertaking given by a person that the person will,\nin order to comply with this Act, take specified action;\n\n(b) a written undertaking given by a person that the person will,\nin order to comply with this Act, refrain from taking\nspecified action;\n\n(c) a written undertaking given by a person that the person will\ntake specified action directed towards ensuring that the\nperson does not contravene this Act, or is unlikely to\ncontravene this Act, in the future.\n\n(2) The undertaking must be expressed to be an undertaking under this\nsection.\n\nEnforceable undertakings  Schedule 10\n\nTelecommunications Legislation Amendment (Competition and Consumer Issues) Act 2005\nNo. 119, 2005            27\n\n(3) The person may withdraw or vary the undertaking at any time, but\nonly with the consent of the ACMA.\n\n(4) The ACMA may, by written notice given to the person, cancel the\nundertaking.\n\n(5) The ACMA may publish the undertaking on its Internet site.\n\n(6) In this section:\nthis Act includes the Telecommunications (Consumer Protection\nand Service Standards) Act 1999.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The ACMA may accept any of the following undertakings:\n\n(a) a written undertaking given by a person that the person will,\nin order to comply with this Act, take specified action;\n\n(b) a written undertaking given by a person that the person will,\nin order to comply with this Act, refrain from taking\nspecified action;\n\n(c) a written undertaking given by a person that the person will\ntake specified action directed towards ensuring that the\nperson does not contravene this Act, or is unlikely to\ncontravene this Act, in the future.\n\n(2) The undertaking must be expressed to be an undertaking under this\nsection.\n\nEnforceable undertakings  Schedule 10\n\nTelecommunications Legislation Amendment (Competition and Consumer Issues) Act 2005\nNo. 119, 2005            27\n\n(3) The person may withdraw or vary the undertaking at any time, but\nonly with the consent of the ACMA.\n\n(4) The ACMA may, by written notice given to the person, cancel the\nundertaking.\n\n(5) The ACMA may publish the undertaking on its Internet site.\n\n(6) In this section:\nthis Act includes the Telecommunications (Consumer Protection\nand Service Standards) Act 1999.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-issues-act-2005-sch-10-sec-572b-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-issues-act-2005-sch-10-sec-572b-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-issues-act-2005-sch-10-sec-572b-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-issues-act-2005-sch-10-sec-572b-ss-4"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-issues-act-2005-sch-10-sec-572b-ss-5"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-issues-act-2005-sch-10-sec-572b-ss-6"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "7f3fadab68711c02bf681b0315d66c5159d5afb3777108197cdd92ca73f11dc9"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-issues-act-2005#sch-10-sec-572b",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "572B Acceptance of undertakings",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 30,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The ACMA may accept any of the following undertakings:\n\n(a) a written undertaking given by a person that the person will,\nin order to comply with this Act, take specified action;\n\n(b) a written undertaking given by a person that the person will,\nin order to comply with this Act, refrain from taking\nspecified action;\n\n(c) a written undertaking given by a person that the person will\ntake specified action directed towards ensuring that the\nperson does not contravene this Act, or is unlikely to\ncontravene this Act, in the future.\n\n(2) The undertaking must be expressed to be an undertaking under this\nsection.\n\nEnforceable undertakings  Schedule 10\n\nTelecommunications Legislation Amendment (Competition and Consumer Issues) Act 2005\nNo. 119, 2005            27\n\n(3) The person may withdraw or vary the undertaking at any time, but\nonly with the consent of the ACMA.\n\n(4) The ACMA may, by written notice given to the person, cancel the\nundertaking.\n\n(5) The ACMA may publish the undertaking on its Internet site.\n\n(6) In this section:\nthis Act includes the Telecommunications (Consumer Protection\nand Service Standards) Act 1999."
    },
