      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-issues-act-2005.pdf, p.31",
      "values:originalText": "(1) If:\n\n(a) a person has given an undertaking under section 572B; and\n\n(b) the undertaking has not been withdrawn or cancelled; and\n\n(c) the ACMA considers that the person has breached the\nundertaking;\nthe ACMA may apply to the Federal Court for an order under\nsubsection (2).",
      "skos:definition": "(1) If:\n\n(a) a person has given an undertaking under section 572B; and\n\n(b) the undertaking has not been withdrawn or cancelled; and\n\n(c) the ACMA considers that the person has breached the\nundertaking;\nthe ACMA may apply to the Federal Court for an order under\nsubsection (2).",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-issues-act-2005-sch-10-sec-572c"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-issues-act-2005-sch-10-sec-572c-ss-1-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-issues-act-2005-sch-10-sec-572c-ss-1-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "466b5a7845b82ccd957807d207c0715e705c71d0a39fe5063401f538ea258653",
      "skos:note": "Enforcement of breach of undertaking"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-issues-act-2005#sch-10-sec-572c-ss-1",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "572C(1) Enforcement of undertakings",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 31,
      "values:originalText": "(1) If:\n\n(a) a person has given an undertaking under section 572B; and\n\n(b) the undertaking has not been withdrawn or cancelled; and\n\n(c) the ACMA considers that the person has breached the\nundertaking;\nthe ACMA may apply to the Federal Court for an order under\nsubsection (2)."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-issues-act-2005-sch-10-sec-572c-ss-1-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-issues-act-2005-sch-10-sec-572c-ss-1"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:Agent"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-issues-act-2005-sch-10-sec-572c-ss-1-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "may",
      "cml:logicSummary": "May apply to Federal Court for order",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "ACMA considers breach",
      "cml:conclusionText": "Order under subsection (2)"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-issues-act-2005-sch-10-sec-572c-ss-2",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "572C(2) Enforcement of undertakings",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-issues-act-2005#sch-10-sec-572c-ss-2"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-issues-act-2005.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-issues-act-2005.pdf, p.31",
      "values:originalText": "(2) If the Federal Court is satisfied that the person has breached the\nundertaking, the Court may make any or all of the following\norders:\n\n(a) an order directing the person to comply with the undertaking;\n\n(b) an order directing the person to pay to the Commonwealth an\namount up to the amount of any financial benefit that the\nperson has obtained directly or indirectly and that is\nreasonably attributable to the breach;\n\n(c) any order that the Court considers appropriate directing the\nperson to compensate any other person who has suffered loss\nor damage as a result of the breach;\n\n(d) any other order that the Court considers appropriate.\n\nSchedule 11  Operational separation of Telstra",
      "skos:definition": "(2) If the Federal Court is satisfied that the person has breached the\nundertaking, the Court may make any or all of the following\norders:\n\n(a) an order directing the person to comply with the undertaking;\n\n(b) an order directing the person to pay to the Commonwealth an\namount up to the amount of any financial benefit that the\nperson has obtained directly or indirectly and that is\nreasonably attributable to the breach;\n\n(c) any order that the Court considers appropriate directing the\nperson to compensate any other person who has suffered loss\nor damage as a result of the breach;\n\n(d) any other order that the Court considers appropriate.\n\nSchedule 11  Operational separation of Telstra",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-issues-act-2005-sch-10-sec-572c"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-issues-act-2005-sch-10-sec-572c-ss-2-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-issues-act-2005-sch-10-sec-572c-ss-2-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "ec500b6c3d14ecae4d202312edfe950abeaf9883f258ae664ba1e2e571b9341b",
      "skos:note": "Court may order person to comply with undertaking."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-issues-act-2005#sch-10-sec-572c-ss-2",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "572C(2) Enforcement of undertakings",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 31,
      "values:originalText": "(2) If the Federal Court is satisfied that the person has breached the\nundertaking, the Court may make any or all of the following\norders:\n\n(a) an order directing the person to comply with the undertaking;\n\n(b) an order directing the person to pay to the Commonwealth an\namount up to the amount of any financial benefit that the\nperson has obtained directly or indirectly and that is\nreasonably attributable to the breach;\n\n(c) any order that the Court considers appropriate directing the\nperson to compensate any other person who has suffered loss\nor damage as a result of the breach;\n\n(d) any other order that the Court considers appropriate.\n\nSchedule 11  Operational separation of Telstra"
    },
