      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-issues-act-2005.pdf, p.32",
      "values:originalText": "(2) At any time after the last day on which a report of a subsection\n61A(1) review was tabled in a House of the Parliament, the\nMinister may, by written instrument, declare that Part 8 of\nSchedule 1 ceases to have effect on a specified day. The specified\nday must not be earlier than the last day on which a resolution\ndisallowing the declaration could have been passed by a House of\nthe Parliament under section 42 of the Legislative Instruments Act\n2003.\nNote:\nA subsection 61A(1) review must be conducted before 1 July 2009.",
      "skos:definition": "(2) At any time after the last day on which a report of a subsection\n61A(1) review was tabled in a House of the Parliament, the\nMinister may, by written instrument, declare that Part 8 of\nSchedule 1 ceases to have effect on a specified day. The specified\nday must not be earlier than the last day on which a resolution\ndisallowing the declaration could have been passed by a House of\nthe Parliament under section 42 of the Legislative Instruments Act\n2003.\nNote:\nA subsection 61A(1) review must be conducted before 1 July 2009.",
      "values:partOf": {
