    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-issues-act-2005-sch-11-sec-61a",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "61A Review before 1 July 2009 of conditions relating to operational",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-issues-act-2005#sch-11-sec-61a"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-issues-act-2005.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-issues-act-2005.pdf, p.32",
      "values:originalText": "separation of Telstra\n\n(1) Before 1 July 2009, the Minister must cause to be conducted a\nreview of the operation of Part 8 of Schedule 1.\n\n(2) A review under subsection (1) must have regard to the following\nmatters:\n\n(a) the state of competition in telecommunications markets;\n\nOperational separation of Telstra  Schedule 11\n\nTelecommunications Legislation Amendment (Competition and Consumer Issues) Act 2005\nNo. 119, 2005            29\n\n(b) whether Telstra has a substantial degree of power in any\ntelecommunications market;\n\n(c) technological developments that have, or might reasonably\nbe expected to have, a significant impact on competition in\ntelecommunications markets;\n\n(d) Telstra’s commercial incentives for supplying wholesale\neligible services;\n\n(e) costs and benefits of the operation of Part 8 of Schedule 1.\n\n(3) The Minister must cause to be prepared a report of a review under\nsubsection (1).\n\n(4) The Minister must cause copies of the report to be tabled in each\nHouse of the Parliament within 15 sitting days of that House after\nthe completion of the preparation of the report.\n\n(5) In this section:\neligible service has the same meaning as in section 152AL of the\nTrade Practices Act 1974.\nsubstantial degree of power in a telecommunications market has\nthe same meaning as in Part XIB of the Trade Practices Act 1974.\ntelecommunications market has the same meaning as in Part XIB\nof the Trade Practices Act 1974.",
      "skos:definition": "separation of Telstra\n\n(1) Before 1 July 2009, the Minister must cause to be conducted a\nreview of the operation of Part 8 of Schedule 1.\n\n(2) A review under subsection (1) must have regard to the following\nmatters:\n\n(a) the state of competition in telecommunications markets;\n\nOperational separation of Telstra  Schedule 11\n\nTelecommunications Legislation Amendment (Competition and Consumer Issues) Act 2005\nNo. 119, 2005            29\n\n(b) whether Telstra has a substantial degree of power in any\ntelecommunications market;\n\n(c) technological developments that have, or might reasonably\nbe expected to have, a significant impact on competition in\ntelecommunications markets;\n\n(d) Telstra’s commercial incentives for supplying wholesale\neligible services;\n\n(e) costs and benefits of the operation of Part 8 of Schedule 1.\n\n(3) The Minister must cause to be prepared a report of a review under\nsubsection (1).\n\n(4) The Minister must cause copies of the report to be tabled in each\nHouse of the Parliament within 15 sitting days of that House after\nthe completion of the preparation of the report.\n\n(5) In this section:\neligible service has the same meaning as in section 152AL of the\nTrade Practices Act 1974.\nsubstantial degree of power in a telecommunications market has\nthe same meaning as in Part XIB of the Trade Practices Act 1974.\ntelecommunications market has the same meaning as in Part XIB\nof the Trade Practices Act 1974.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-issues-act-2005-sch-11-sec-61a-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-issues-act-2005-sch-11-sec-61a-ss-2"
        },
