        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-issues-act-2005-sch-11-sec-2005-ss-6"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "fdeca138de46abb9b2a00f0fa193d24af3e7e78709b6dc4b9886dd68a943d844"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-issues-act-2005#sch-11-sec-2005",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "2005 No. 119, 2005",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 34,
      "values:originalText": "(a) a direction that Telstra implement effective administrative\nsystems for monitoring compliance with the condition;\n\n(b) a direction that Telstra implement a system designed to give\nTelstra’s employees, agents and contractors a reasonable\nknowledge and understanding of the requirements of the\ncondition, in so far as those requirements affect the\nemployees, agents or contractors concerned.\n\n(4) Telstra must not contravene a direction under subsection (2).\n\n(5) A direction under subsection (2) is not a legislative instrument for\nthe purposes of the Legislative Instruments Act 2003.\n\n(6) This section does not limit section 69."
    },
