      },
      "cml:premiseText": "(1) The aim of this Part is..."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-issues-act-2005-sch-11-sec-48-ss-2",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "48(2) Aim and objects",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-issues-act-2005#sch-11-sec-48-ss-2"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-issues-act-2005.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-issues-act-2005.pdf, p.36",
      "values:originalText": "(2) The objects of this Part are as follows:\n\n(a) to promote a principle of equivalence in relation to the supply\nby Telstra of designated services to:\n\n(i) Telstra’s wholesale customers; and\n\n(ii) Telstra’s retail business units;\n\n(b) to require Telstra to maintain the following business units:\n\n(i) one or more wholesale business units;\n\n(ii) one or more retail business units;\n\n(iii) one or more key network services business units;\n\n(c) to promote a substantial degree of organisational and\noperational separation between:\n\n(i) Telstra’s wholesale business units (considered as a\ngroup); and\n\n(ii) Telstra’s retail business units (considered as a group);\nand\n\n(iii) Telstra’s key network services business units\n(considered as a group);\n\n(d) to promote responsiveness by Telstra in meeting its\nwholesale customers’ needs in relation to eligible services;\n\n(e) to require Telstra to have a plan (to be known as the final\noperational separation plan) to achieve the aim and other\nobjects of this Part;\n\nOperational separation of Telstra  Schedule 11\n\nTelecommunications Legislation Amendment (Competition and Consumer Issues) Act 2005\nNo. 119, 2005            33\n\n(f) to ensure that Telstra has systems, procedures and processes\nthat promote and facilitate:\n\n(i) compliance with the final operational separation plan;\nand\n\n(ii) monitoring of, and reporting on, compliance with the\nplan; and\n\n(iii) the development of performance measures relating to\ncompliance with the plan; and\n\n(iv) audit, and other checks, of compliance with the plan;\n\n(g) to ensure that the achievement of:\n\n(i) the aim of this Part; and\n\n(ii) any of the above objects;\n\ndoes not impair Telstra’s ability to compete on a fair and\nefficient basis.",
      "skos:definition": "(2) The objects of this Part are as follows:\n\n(a) to promote a principle of equivalence in relation to the supply\nby Telstra of designated services to:\n\n(i) Telstra’s wholesale customers; and\n\n(ii) Telstra’s retail business units;\n\n(b) to require Telstra to maintain the following business units:\n\n(i) one or more wholesale business units;\n\n(ii) one or more retail business units;\n\n(iii) one or more key network services business units;\n\n(c) to promote a substantial degree of organisational and\noperational separation between:\n\n(i) Telstra’s wholesale business units (considered as a\ngroup); and\n\n(ii) Telstra’s retail business units (considered as a group);\nand\n\n(iii) Telstra’s key network services business units\n(considered as a group);\n\n(d) to promote responsiveness by Telstra in meeting its\nwholesale customers’ needs in relation to eligible services;\n\n(e) to require Telstra to have a plan (to be known as the final\noperational separation plan) to achieve the aim and other\nobjects of this Part;\n\nOperational separation of Telstra  Schedule 11\n\nTelecommunications Legislation Amendment (Competition and Consumer Issues) Act 2005\nNo. 119, 2005            33\n\n(f) to ensure that Telstra has systems, procedures and processes\nthat promote and facilitate:\n\n(i) compliance with the final operational separation plan;\nand\n\n(ii) monitoring of, and reporting on, compliance with the\nplan; and\n\n(iii) the development of performance measures relating to\ncompliance with the plan; and\n\n(iv) audit, and other checks, of compliance with the plan;\n\n(g) to ensure that the achievement of:\n\n(i) the aim of this Part; and\n\n(ii) any of the above objects;\n\ndoes not impair Telstra’s ability to compete on a fair and\nefficient basis.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-issues-act-2005-sch-11-sec-48"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-issues-act-2005-sch-11-sec-48-ss-2-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-issues-act-2005-sch-11-sec-48-ss-2-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "db8248133c5d7413f5b0b3f50ccd627135cb8a83ccf0ec8522257a3616e20c3e",
      "skos:note": "Promote a principle of equivalence in relation to the supply by Telstra of designated services."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-issues-act-2005#sch-11-sec-48-ss-2",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "48(2) Aim and objects",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 36,
      "values:originalText": "(2) The objects of this Part are as follows:\n\n(a) to promote a principle of equivalence in relation to the supply\nby Telstra of designated services to:\n\n(i) Telstra’s wholesale customers; and\n\n(ii) Telstra’s retail business units;\n\n(b) to require Telstra to maintain the following business units:\n\n(i) one or more wholesale business units;\n\n(ii) one or more retail business units;\n\n(iii) one or more key network services business units;\n\n(c) to promote a substantial degree of organisational and\noperational separation between:\n\n(i) Telstra’s wholesale business units (considered as a\ngroup); and\n\n(ii) Telstra’s retail business units (considered as a group);\nand\n\n(iii) Telstra’s key network services business units\n(considered as a group);\n\n(d) to promote responsiveness by Telstra in meeting its\nwholesale customers’ needs in relation to eligible services;\n\n(e) to require Telstra to have a plan (to be known as the final\noperational separation plan) to achieve the aim and other\nobjects of this Part;\n\nOperational separation of Telstra  Schedule 11\n\nTelecommunications Legislation Amendment (Competition and Consumer Issues) Act 2005\nNo. 119, 2005            33\n\n(f) to ensure that Telstra has systems, procedures and processes\nthat promote and facilitate:\n\n(i) compliance with the final operational separation plan;\nand\n\n(ii) monitoring of, and reporting on, compliance with the\nplan; and\n\n(iii) the development of performance measures relating to\ncompliance with the plan; and\n\n(iv) audit, and other checks, of compliance with the plan;\n\n(g) to ensure that the achievement of:\n\n(i) the aim of this Part; and\n\n(ii) any of the above objects;\n\ndoes not impair Telstra’s ability to compete on a fair and\nefficient basis."
    },
