    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-issues-act-2005-sch-11-sec-48-ss-5",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "48(5) Aim and objects",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-issues-act-2005#sch-11-sec-48-ss-5"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-issues-act-2005.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-issues-act-2005.pdf, p.36",
      "values:originalText": "(5) In determining, for the purposes of paragraph (2)(d), the needs of\nTelstra’s wholesale customers in relation to eligible services,\nregard must be had to the following needs:\n\n(a) the need for those customers to be supplied by Telstra with\neligible services on a basis that allows fair competition with\neligible services supplied by Telstra’s retail business units;\n\n(b) the need for disputes between those customers and Telstra\nabout eligible services to be resolved in a fair and timely\nmanner;\n\n(c) the need for confidentiality in relation to eligible services\nsupplied by Telstra to those customers;\n\n(d) the need to be kept informed of relevant issues and\ndevelopments in connection with:\n\n(i) Telstra’s network, in so far as it relates to the supply of\neligible services; and\n\n(ii) eligible services supplied by Telstra.\n\nSchedule 11  Operational separation of Telstra",
      "skos:definition": "(5) In determining, for the purposes of paragraph (2)(d), the needs of\nTelstra’s wholesale customers in relation to eligible services,\nregard must be had to the following needs:\n\n(a) the need for those customers to be supplied by Telstra with\neligible services on a basis that allows fair competition with\neligible services supplied by Telstra’s retail business units;\n\n(b) the need for disputes between those customers and Telstra\nabout eligible services to be resolved in a fair and timely\nmanner;\n\n(c) the need for confidentiality in relation to eligible services\nsupplied by Telstra to those customers;\n\n(d) the need to be kept informed of relevant issues and\ndevelopments in connection with:\n\n(i) Telstra’s network, in so far as it relates to the supply of\neligible services; and\n\n(ii) eligible services supplied by Telstra.\n\nSchedule 11  Operational separation of Telstra",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-issues-act-2005-sch-11-sec-48"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-issues-act-2005-sch-11-sec-48-ss-5-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-issues-act-2005-sch-11-sec-48-ss-5-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "3050cb02efc126f75f11a49bed87d63ed54ca230c2e2543b0e82cd95d9476f5a",
      "skos:note": "Must consider the needs of wholesale customers in relation to eligible services."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-issues-act-2005#sch-11-sec-48-ss-5",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "48(5) Aim and objects",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 36,
      "values:originalText": "(5) In determining, for the purposes of paragraph (2)(d), the needs of\nTelstra’s wholesale customers in relation to eligible services,\nregard must be had to the following needs:\n\n(a) the need for those customers to be supplied by Telstra with\neligible services on a basis that allows fair competition with\neligible services supplied by Telstra’s retail business units;\n\n(b) the need for disputes between those customers and Telstra\nabout eligible services to be resolved in a fair and timely\nmanner;\n\n(c) the need for confidentiality in relation to eligible services\nsupplied by Telstra to those customers;\n\n(d) the need to be kept informed of relevant issues and\ndevelopments in connection with:\n\n(i) Telstra’s network, in so far as it relates to the supply of\neligible services; and\n\n(ii) eligible services supplied by Telstra.\n\nSchedule 11  Operational separation of Telstra"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-issues-act-2005-sch-11-sec-48-ss-5-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-issues-act-2005-sch-11-sec-48-ss-5"
