    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-issues-act-2005-sch-11-sec-50a",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "50A Designated services",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-issues-act-2005#sch-11-sec-50a"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-issues-act-2005.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-issues-act-2005.pdf, p.39",
      "values:originalText": "(1) For the purposes of this Part, a designated service is an eligible\nservice specified in a written determination made by the Minister\nunder this subclause.\n\n(2) The Minister must not make a determination under subclause (1)\nthat specifies a service that is not an active declared service (within\nthe meaning of section 152AR of the Trade Practices Act 1974)\nunless:\n\n(a) the determination is the first determination made under\nsubclause (1); or\n\n(b) Telstra has given written consent to the making of the\ndetermination.\n\n(3) Subsection 33(3) of the Acts Interpretation Act 1901 applies to a\npower conferred on the Minister by subclause (1), but it applies\nwith the change set out in subclause (4).\n\nSchedule 11  Operational separation of Telstra",
      "skos:definition": "(1) For the purposes of this Part, a designated service is an eligible\nservice specified in a written determination made by the Minister\nunder this subclause.\n\n(2) The Minister must not make a determination under subclause (1)\nthat specifies a service that is not an active declared service (within\nthe meaning of section 152AR of the Trade Practices Act 1974)\nunless:\n\n(a) the determination is the first determination made under\nsubclause (1); or\n\n(b) Telstra has given written consent to the making of the\ndetermination.\n\n(3) Subsection 33(3) of the Acts Interpretation Act 1901 applies to a\npower conferred on the Minister by subclause (1), but it applies\nwith the change set out in subclause (4).\n\nSchedule 11  Operational separation of Telstra",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-issues-act-2005-sch-11-sec-50a-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-issues-act-2005-sch-11-sec-50a-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-issues-act-2005-sch-11-sec-50a-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "a092ed35717b4d7b229ad8cc02fc003b76bb2af42759c88d1eaf0ea63cb0f586"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-issues-act-2005#sch-11-sec-50a",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "50A Designated services",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 39,
      "values:originalText": "(1) For the purposes of this Part, a designated service is an eligible\nservice specified in a written determination made by the Minister\nunder this subclause.\n\n(2) The Minister must not make a determination under subclause (1)\nthat specifies a service that is not an active declared service (within\nthe meaning of section 152AR of the Trade Practices Act 1974)\nunless:\n\n(a) the determination is the first determination made under\nsubclause (1); or\n\n(b) Telstra has given written consent to the making of the\ndetermination.\n\n(3) Subsection 33(3) of the Acts Interpretation Act 1901 applies to a\npower conferred on the Minister by subclause (1), but it applies\nwith the change set out in subclause (4).\n\nSchedule 11  Operational separation of Telstra"
    },
