    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-issues-act-2005-sch-11-sec-54",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "54 Approval of draft by Minister",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-issues-act-2005#sch-11-sec-54"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-issues-act-2005.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-issues-act-2005.pdf, p.42",
      "values:originalText": "(1) This clause applies if Telstra gives the Minister a draft operational\nseparation plan.\n\n(2) The Minister must:\n\n(a) approve the plan; or\n\n(b) refuse to approve the plan.\n\n(3) In deciding whether to approve the plan, the Minister must have\nregard to the following matters:\n\n(a) the extent to which the plan is likely to achieve the aim and\nobjects of this Part; and\n\n(b) such other matters (if any) as are specified in a written\ndetermination made by the Minister under this paragraph.\n\n(4) Subclause (3) does not limit the matters to which the Minister may\nhave regard.\n\n(5) If the Minister neither approves, nor refuses to approve, the plan\nbefore the end of the period of 90 days after the day on which the\nMinister received the draft plan, the Minister is taken, at the end of\nthat period, to have approved the plan under subclause (2).\n\n(6) As soon as practicable after deciding whether to approve the plan,\nthe Minister must notify Telstra in writing of the decision.\n\nOperational separation of Telstra  Schedule 11\n\nTelecommunications Legislation Amendment (Competition and Consumer Issues) Act 2005\nNo. 119, 2005            39\n\n(7) If the Minister refuses to approve the plan, the Minister must notify\nTelstra in writing of the Minister’s reasons for the refusal.\n\n(8) If the Minister refuses to approve the plan, the Minister may, by\nwritten notice given to Telstra, direct Telstra to:\n\n(a) vary the draft plan in accordance with the direction; and\n\n(b) give the varied draft plan to the Minister under subclause (1).\nTelstra must give the varied draft plan to the Minister within 60\ndays after the day on which the direction was given.\n\n(9) A determination under paragraph (3)(b) is a legislative instrument\nfor the purposes of the Legislative Instruments Act 2003.\n\n(10) A direction under subclause (8) is a legislative instrument for the\npurposes of the Legislative Instruments Act 2003.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) This clause applies if Telstra gives the Minister a draft operational\nseparation plan.\n\n(2) The Minister must:\n\n(a) approve the plan; or\n\n(b) refuse to approve the plan.\n\n(3) In deciding whether to approve the plan, the Minister must have\nregard to the following matters:\n\n(a) the extent to which the plan is likely to achieve the aim and\nobjects of this Part; and\n\n(b) such other matters (if any) as are specified in a written\ndetermination made by the Minister under this paragraph.\n\n(4) Subclause (3) does not limit the matters to which the Minister may\nhave regard.\n\n(5) If the Minister neither approves, nor refuses to approve, the plan\nbefore the end of the period of 90 days after the day on which the\nMinister received the draft plan, the Minister is taken, at the end of\nthat period, to have approved the plan under subclause (2).\n\n(6) As soon as practicable after deciding whether to approve the plan,\nthe Minister must notify Telstra in writing of the decision.\n\nOperational separation of Telstra  Schedule 11\n\nTelecommunications Legislation Amendment (Competition and Consumer Issues) Act 2005\nNo. 119, 2005            39\n\n(7) If the Minister refuses to approve the plan, the Minister must notify\nTelstra in writing of the Minister’s reasons for the refusal.\n\n(8) If the Minister refuses to approve the plan, the Minister may, by\nwritten notice given to Telstra, direct Telstra to:\n\n(a) vary the draft plan in accordance with the direction; and\n\n(b) give the varied draft plan to the Minister under subclause (1).\nTelstra must give the varied draft plan to the Minister within 60\ndays after the day on which the direction was given.\n\n(9) A determination under paragraph (3)(b) is a legislative instrument\nfor the purposes of the Legislative Instruments Act 2003.\n\n(10) A direction under subclause (8) is a legislative instrument for the\npurposes of the Legislative Instruments Act 2003.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-issues-act-2005-sch-11-sec-54-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-issues-act-2005-sch-11-sec-54-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-issues-act-2005-sch-11-sec-54-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-issues-act-2005-sch-11-sec-54-ss-4"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-issues-act-2005-sch-11-sec-54-ss-5"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-issues-act-2005-sch-11-sec-54-ss-6"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-issues-act-2005-sch-11-sec-54-ss-7"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-issues-act-2005-sch-11-sec-54-ss-8"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-issues-act-2005-sch-11-sec-54-ss-9"
        },
        {
