    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-issues-act-2005-sch-11-sec-56",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "56 Variation of final operational separation plan",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-issues-act-2005#sch-11-sec-56"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-issues-act-2005.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-issues-act-2005.pdf, p.43",
      "values:originalText": "(1) This clause applies if:\n\n(a) a final operational separation plan is in force; and\n\n(b) Telstra gives the Minister a draft variation of the plan.\n\n(2) The Minister must:\n\n(a) approve the variation; or\n\n(b) refuse to approve the variation.\n\n(3) In deciding whether to approve the variation, the Minister must\nhave regard to the following matters:\n\nSchedule 11  Operational separation of Telstra",
      "skos:definition": "(1) This clause applies if:\n\n(a) a final operational separation plan is in force; and\n\n(b) Telstra gives the Minister a draft variation of the plan.\n\n(2) The Minister must:\n\n(a) approve the variation; or\n\n(b) refuse to approve the variation.\n\n(3) In deciding whether to approve the variation, the Minister must\nhave regard to the following matters:\n\nSchedule 11  Operational separation of Telstra",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-issues-act-2005-sch-11-sec-56-ss-1"
        },
