    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-issues-act-2005-sch-11-sec-59",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "59 Contents of draft or final rectification plan",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-issues-act-2005#sch-11-sec-59"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-issues-act-2005.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-issues-act-2005.pdf, p.46",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The following matters must be set out in each draft or final\nrectification plan that relates to a contravention of a final\noperational separation plan:\n\n(a) the action to be taken by Telstra to ensure that the\ncontravention ceases;\n\n(b) the action to be taken by Telstra directed towards ensuring\nthat there is no repetition of the contravention in the future;\n\n(c) the action to be taken by Telstra by way of reporting to the\nMinister on any action taken by it as mentioned in\nparagraph (a) or (b).\nNote:\nA final rectification plan is a draft rectification plan that has been\napproved by the Minister—see clause 62.\n\n(2) A draft or final rectification plan may make provision for, or in\nrelation to, a matter by empowering the Minister, the ACCC or the\nACMA to make decisions of an administrative character.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The following matters must be set out in each draft or final\nrectification plan that relates to a contravention of a final\noperational separation plan:\n\n(a) the action to be taken by Telstra to ensure that the\ncontravention ceases;\n\n(b) the action to be taken by Telstra directed towards ensuring\nthat there is no repetition of the contravention in the future;\n\n(c) the action to be taken by Telstra by way of reporting to the\nMinister on any action taken by it as mentioned in\nparagraph (a) or (b).\nNote:\nA final rectification plan is a draft rectification plan that has been\napproved by the Minister—see clause 62.\n\n(2) A draft or final rectification plan may make provision for, or in\nrelation to, a matter by empowering the Minister, the ACCC or the\nACMA to make decisions of an administrative character.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-issues-act-2005-sch-11-sec-59-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-issues-act-2005-sch-11-sec-59-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "5811d7cc80c0868c42274d7d4cd8f54f8a56e3a6b2cfd57f0df60af705085349"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-issues-act-2005#sch-11-sec-59",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "59 Contents of draft or final rectification plan",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 46,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The following matters must be set out in each draft or final\nrectification plan that relates to a contravention of a final\noperational separation plan:\n\n(a) the action to be taken by Telstra to ensure that the\ncontravention ceases;\n\n(b) the action to be taken by Telstra directed towards ensuring\nthat there is no repetition of the contravention in the future;\n\n(c) the action to be taken by Telstra by way of reporting to the\nMinister on any action taken by it as mentioned in\nparagraph (a) or (b).\nNote:\nA final rectification plan is a draft rectification plan that has been\napproved by the Minister—see clause 62.\n\n(2) A draft or final rectification plan may make provision for, or in\nrelation to, a matter by empowering the Minister, the ACCC or the\nACMA to make decisions of an administrative character."
    },
