      "cml:premiseText": "(10) A variation of a final rectification plan is not a legislative instrument for the purposes of the Legislative Instruments Act 2003.",
      "cml:conclusionText": "If a variation of a final rectification plan is not classified as a legislative instrument, then it implies an obligation to comply with the Act."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-issues-act-2005-sch-11-sec-64",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "64 Minister may direct Telstra to vary final rectification plan",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-issues-act-2005#sch-11-sec-64"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-issues-act-2005.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-issues-act-2005.pdf, p.49",
      "values:originalText": "(1) This clause applies if a final rectification plan is in force.\n\n(2) The Minister may, by written notice given to Telstra, direct Telstra\nto:\n\n(a) prepare a draft variation of the plan in accordance with the\ndirection; and\n\n(b) give the draft variation to the Minister under subclause 63(1).\nThe draft variation must be given to the Minister within 60 days\nafter the day on which the direction was given.\n\n(3) A direction under this clause is a legislative instrument for the\npurposes of the Legislative Instruments Act 2003.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) This clause applies if a final rectification plan is in force.\n\n(2) The Minister may, by written notice given to Telstra, direct Telstra\nto:\n\n(a) prepare a draft variation of the plan in accordance with the\ndirection; and\n\n(b) give the draft variation to the Minister under subclause 63(1).\nThe draft variation must be given to the Minister within 60 days\nafter the day on which the direction was given.\n\n(3) A direction under this clause is a legislative instrument for the\npurposes of the Legislative Instruments Act 2003.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-issues-act-2005-sch-11-sec-64-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-issues-act-2005-sch-11-sec-64-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-issues-act-2005-sch-11-sec-64-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "7959c94107a331f5b2c0f6beebb8c3c3daf5d6a8b9fa5bd1f470966033166980"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-issues-act-2005#sch-11-sec-64",
